{% set local_problem %}
<p>A lot of Albertville homes have gutters that are past their prime. Some are original to houses built 40-50 years ago. Others were installed cheap — sectional gutters from the hardware store, put up by whoever was available.</p>

<p>The problem with sectional gutters is the seams. Every 10 feet, there's a joint held together by caulk or crimped metal. Those joints leak. They also catch debris, which leads to clogs. And Alabama's temperature swings — hot summers, occasional freezes — make the seams work loose over time.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters solve this by eliminating the seams entirely. One continuous piece of aluminum from corner to corner. No joints to leak, no gaps to catch debris, no weak points to fail. For Albertville homeowners who want gutters that just work, seamless is the way to go.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are made from a continuous roll of aluminum, formed on-site to the exact length you need. Instead of 10-foot sections connected together, you get one piece that runs the entire length of each gutter run on your home.</p>

<p>We bring a portable gutter machine to your house, feed in the aluminum coil, and out comes a custom gutter that fits your home exactly. The only joints are at corners and downspout connections — not every 10 feet like sectional gutters.</p>

<p>The result is a cleaner look, better performance, and longer life. Seamless gutters typically last 20+ years with minimal maintenance. Sectional gutters? You'll be patching seams and dealing with leaks long before that.</p>
{% endset %}

